principal|most-important|ADJECTIVE|Most important|Most important or main among the things being discussed.|chính; chủ yếu|The principal reason for the delay was a damaged bridge.|Nguyên nhân chính của sự chậm trễ là một cây cầu bị hư hại.|Usually before a noun; principal aim, principal cause. Principle is a different noun meaning a rule or belief.|0
principal|head-of-an-educational-institution|NOUN|Head of an educational institution|The person in charge of a school or certain other educational institutions.|hiệu trưởng|The principal welcomed the new pupils at the assembly.|Hiệu trưởng chào đón các học sinh mới trong buổi sinh hoạt chung.|Countable; school principal. Titles and the use of headteacher vary by country and institution.|1
thus|as-a-result|ADVERB|As a result|For that reason or as a consequence of what has just been stated.|do đó; vì vậy|The path was flooded; thus, the walkers chose a longer route.|Lối đi bị ngập; do đó, những người đi bộ chọn một đường dài hơn.|Formal connecting adverb. Join full clauses with a full stop or semicolon rather than treating thus as an ordinary coordinating conjunction.|0
thus|in-this-way|ADVERB|In this way|In the manner just described or shown.|như vậy; theo cách này|Fold the corners thus, and the paper will form a small tray.|Gấp các góc theo cách này, và tờ giấy sẽ tạo thành một chiếc khay nhỏ.|Formal or literary manner adverb; often accompanies a description or demonstration.|1
watch|look-attentively|VERB|Look attentively|To look at something for a period of time, paying attention to what happens.|xem; theo dõi|We watched the boat pass under the low bridge.|Chúng tôi nhìn chiếc thuyền đi qua dưới cây cầu thấp.|Watch, watched, watching; watch someone do or doing something. Watch emphasizes attention over time.|0
watch|wrist-timepiece|NOUN|Wrist timepiece|A small device for showing the time, usually worn on the wrist.|đồng hồ đeo tay|His watch stopped during the journey, so he checked the station clock.|Đồng hồ đeo tay của anh ấy dừng trong chuyến đi, nên anh ấy xem đồng hồ ở nhà ga.|Countable; a wristwatch, a pocket watch. Clock generally names a larger timepiece.|1
might|uncertain-possibility|VERB|Uncertain possibility|Used to say that something is possible but not certain.|có thể; có lẽ sẽ|The delivery might arrive this afternoon if the road reopens.|Hàng giao có thể đến chiều nay nếu đường mở lại.|Modal auxiliary followed by the base verb; no third-person -s. Might not expresses possible non-occurrence.|0
might|great-power|NOUN|Great power|Great strength or power, especially the power of a group or nation.|sức mạnh; uy lực|The story contrasts the empire's military might with the villagers' determination.|Câu chuyện đối chiếu sức mạnh quân sự của đế quốc với quyết tâm của dân làng.|Uncountable, often formal; military might, with all one's might. Distinct from the possibility modal.|-
new|recently-made-or-acquired|ADJECTIVE|Recently made or acquired|Made, obtained or introduced recently, rather than existing for a long time.|mới|The workshop bought a new cutting machine last month.|Xưởng mua một máy cắt mới vào tháng trước.|New equipment, a new idea; new to someone means unfamiliar to them, even if it is old elsewhere.|0
new|inexperienced-in-a-role|ADJECTIVE|Inexperienced in a role|Having only recently started an activity or joined a place and still learning about it.|mới vào; chưa quen|She is new to pottery, so the instructor explained how to prepare the clay.|Cô ấy mới học làm gốm, nên người hướng dẫn giải thích cách chuẩn bị đất sét.|New to a job or activity; new at something is also used. Distinguish a person's experience from an object's age.|1
